From 0261fe8b5a275bdca26d8368574e7758e12c005b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:55:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] avcodec: add ff_ac4_parser

Streaming splitter for the Annex G sync stream plus a TOC prober.

AC41 frames accept on CRC-16 (MSB-first poly 0x8005 over length
bytes, raw frame and stored word, zero remainder). AC40 frames
accept on a chaining anchor (next head parses exactly at the frame
end) or, at EOF, on an exact end plus a valid TOC head. Every
accept also passes a TOC-head gate that rejects the reserved rate
rows 14/15; any reject advances exactly one byte. Sequence-counter
stride is never a criterion. Heads claiming past AC4_MAX_SCAN
(128 KiB) classify as not-a-head before buffering or CRC, bounding
adversarial resync cost.

The TOC probe reports key_frame from b_iframe_global and, when the
bed walk completes, the output-domain (sample_rate, duration) pair
(base sample frequency x sf_mult with exact Table E.1 counts,
N5-consistent, never the internal spf x fps grid; nominal unlocked
phase on 1001-rate rows), channels (IMS presented counts for
cm120/121 with pres_ver 2) and a running bit_rate average. Failures
leave params untouched while the frame still emits. The walk lives in
the new header-only libavcodec/ac4_toc.h (no Makefile change): one
walker, one rate table. The raw demuxer converges onto it in a
follow-up once its goldens can be re-pinned to parser keyflags.

COMPLETE_FRAMES mode passes bare raw frames through untouched and
only probes the TOC; it never scans for sync.

Registration in parsers.c and the Makefile, ac4_demuxer_select in
configure (generic containers select no codec parsers; minimal
mov/mpegts builds enable --enable-parser=ac4 explicitly). Changelog
entry after Series E's line (one policy for the whole submission;
Series D applies stacked).

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
