From da985fdacdf034d3d4032134c5fe783cd6598beb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:14:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fate: add self-contained ac4 ts demux test

Upstream takes no testless demux path: the TS side relied on the
Series E mux+PMT pins plus a codec-id probe, with nothing asserting
demux through in-tree mpegts + ff_ac4_parser. New
api-ac4-ts-demux-test synthesizes its vectors in code (the same
minimal version-2 stereo TOC shape as fate-ac4-parser, wrapped as
Annex G AC41 with CRCs solved per frame), so the suite needs no
uploaded samples and no encoder: pre-encoded synth payloads keep
the Series C encoder dependency out by design (documented choice).

Roundtrip: mux 4x70 B AC41 to MPEG-TS with -mpegts_flags system_b
(via the Series E descriptor path), then assert at the file level
(188 framing, PAT/PMT CRCs, one stream, stream_type 0x06, 'AC-4'
registration, 0x7F/0x15 config-only stereo descriptor) and at the
demux level (1 stream, codec ac4/tag AC-4, pid match, post-parse
48 kHz stereo params, 4 packets == byte-identical payloads). Two
negatives fail loud: every PMT section corrupted (table_id 0x02->0xFF,
id+CRC both break) must not yield an AC-4 stream -- observed shape is
open-ok with codec unknown on pid 0x100 -- and a file cut
mid-PES-payload of frame 3 must yield <4 packets (observed: the 2
whole frames, matched) with the read loop terminating.

Wired as fate-ac4-ts-demux behind MPEGTS_MUXER + MPEGTS_DEMUXER
+ AC4_PARSER, next to fate-ac4-parser/fate-ac4-mp4-roundtrip in
tests/fate/ac4.mak. No mux/demux code changes.

Upstream placement: Series D (parser), not E and not standalone.
The test pins demux+parser behavior (params fill, framing,
negatives); the Series E mux bytes are only the stimulus.

